# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Encyclopedia descriptions, batch E."""
DESC_E = {
    "RT": {
        162: "Based on the Gundam X, this mobile suit was developed by the Government Reconstruction Committee with the aim of creating 'a new Gundam possessing tremendous power as a symbol.'\nIts base was the unit Jamil piloted during the Seventh Space War, but so much cutting-edge technology has been incorporated internally that it can fairly be called an entirely new model. Katock, however, calls it \"a fifteen-year-old ghost.\"\nThe Satellite Cannon, the Gundam X's greatest feature, has been doubled into the Twin Satellite Cannon. Its output has more than doubled as well, making it powerful enough to destroy even the artificial island Zonder Epta or a Colony Laser.\nNot only the Satellite Cannon but the unit's output, mobility, and maneuverability have all seen dramatic improvements across the board. In its first battle, despite fighting alone and without even a rifle, it shot down as many as eight Varients, a testament to its outstanding performance.\nHowever, the dedicated Buster Rifle is no longer integrated with the shield, and this has proven a drawback in terms of durability, leading to it being destroyed on several occasions. Because of this, the pilot was once forced to borrow a rifle from the Gundam Airmaster to keep fighting.",
        163: "The combined form of the Gundam Double X and the G-Falcon.\nThe G-Falcon's B-Parts, moved to the back, function as an energy pack, allowing the Twin Satellite Cannon to fire at maximum output as well as enabling rapid-fire shots.\nThere is also a cruising form in which the Gundam Double X is sandwiched between the G-Falcon's A- and B-Parts; the overall length and weight listed here are those of that configuration.",
        164: "A high-mobility support fighter developed by the old Federation Forces to support Gundam-type mobile suits.\nIt was a prototype that never saw actual combat; left drifting in space in a half-destroyed state, it was recovered and restored for use by Pala and the rest of the anti-Space Revolutionary Army organization Satelicon.\nIt consists of a cockpit section (A-Parts) and a booster section (B-Parts), and by housing (combining with) a Gundam-type mobile suit between the two parts, it can enhance that unit's strengths or compensate for its weaknesses. In practice, however, it combined with the Gundam Double X only a handful of times, combined with the Gundam Leopard Destroy just once as a test, and never combined with the Gundam Airmaster Burst at all.\nEven alone it boasts excellent mobility and firepower, and it distinguished itself by shooting down numerous Septems and Daughtress Neos.\nAlong with the Gundam Double X, it is one of the few units to be named in a subtitle.",
        165: "An Alps-class land battleship captained by Jamil.\nThough officially classified as a 'land battleship,' it can also travel across water via hovering, giving it a wide operational range.\nIt can carry up to six mobile suits, with the Gundam X, Gundam Airmaster, and Gundam Leopard serving as its primary complement.\nIt also serves as a living space for its pilots, including Garrod and the others. When Roabey became a permanent employee aboard the Freeden, she had a relaxation room installed at her own expense to make the voyage more comfortable.",
        166: "A mobile suit used as a mainstay by the Space Revolutionary Army during the Seventh Space War. The unit Ennil uses is an improved model, purchased from Lumark of the Sea Vultures and repainted in her personal color, blue.\nIt has been considerably reinforced in propulsion and other areas compared to a standard Jenice, and thanks in part to Ennil's own skill, it was able to hold its own even against the new-model Varients.\nFor the final battle it was refitted for space combat and launched into space together with the Freeden II.",
        167: "A mobile armor built by Lumark of the Sea Vultures, with whom Ennil was on close terms, out of salvaged parts.\nIts mobility leaves nothing to be desired - when Ennil happened to witness the Gundam Double X and was subsequently pursued by the New Federation Forces, it managed to outrun even the new-model Varient mobile suits. However, due to insufficient firepower it was unable to stand up to a Gundam; it was caught by the Gundam Ashtaron and shot down by the Gundam Vassago.\nThe unit's name means 'hope' in Lumark's native tongue.",
        168: "A mobile suit created by upgrading the Gundam Vassago for space combat.\nModifications extend down to the smallest details, including reinforcement of the Strike Claw's attack power and shock-absorption capacity, and removal of the inner frame's armor.\nThe Mega Sonic Cannon, its greatest feature, has gained an additional two barrels on the chest to become the Triple Mega Sonic Cannon, further sharpening its already fearsome destructive power to match its menacing appearance. The chest armor, shaped to resemble a face, opens when the Triple Mega Sonic Cannon is fired, embodying the unit's name, Chest Break.\nThe Satellite Launcher, used together with the Gundam Ashtaron HC, requires successful control of the Satellite System, but its power rivals that of the Twin Satellite Cannon.",
        169: "A unit created by upgrading the Gundam Ashtaron for space combat.\nIts greatest feature, the 'Trans-System' mechanism for morphing into mobile armor form, remains intact. Not only its defensive strength but also its mobility in mobile armor form is high enough to rival the G-Falcon both within and outside the atmosphere. When morphing, roughly half the unit's body is stored within its greatly enlarged backpack, giving it a shape that embodies its name, Hermit Crab.\nIn addition to the enlarged Atomic Scissors and the change from the Scissors Beam Cannon to the Scissors Cannon, it is also equipped with the Satellite Launcher, though the conditions for its use are demanding - it requires successful control of the Satellite System and can only be used together with the Gundam Vassago CB. This gives it attack power that rivals even the Gundam Double X.",
        170: "A prototype mobile suit developed by the New Federation Forces.\nLike the Gundam-type units, it is equipped with the Flash System, allowing a Newtype pilot to remotely control five Bit Mobile Suits. Unlike the Bit Mobile Suits used by Gundam-type units, the Rashvent's Bit Mobile Suits are identical in appearance to the main unit itself, making it difficult for enemies to single it out in battle.\nPiloted by Abel, whose Newtype abilities blossomed over the course of the fighting, it held its own - and more - against Garrod, Jamil, and Witz all at once.",
        171: "A high-mobility mobile armor developed by the New Federation Forces.\nWith a fighter-jet-like form, a cockpit resembling a mobile suit's head, and a beam rifle gripped at the barrel by a manipulator, its shape stands out considerably compared to other mobile suits and mobile armors.\nDesigned with the goal of securing air superiority, it moderately damaged the Gundam Airmaster in an aerial battle against it.",
        172: "A mobile suit developed by the New Federation Forces as an evolution of the Daughtress.\nThe Wired Beam Rifles mounted on both arms can be used as beam cutters at close range or as beam-firing rifles at medium to long range. Jamil initially read this as a close-combat weapon, believing that \"if he kept his distance, he wouldn't be hit.\" But this assumption was quickly overturned, putting him in a tight spot on one occasion.\nSome units instead carry a standard beam rifle.",
        173: "A mass-production mobile suit that serves as the mainstay of the Space Revolutionary Army.\nIts sturdy, beam-resistant armor kept it from going down easily even under attack from the Gundam Double X or the Gundam Vassago CB.\nDespite its sluggish appearance, it retains high mobility thanks to vernier thrusters mounted throughout the unit. However, it has a weakness in that it becomes fragile if those verniers are targeted; once Garrod discovered this, Croudas began falling one after another.\nUnits piloted by regular soldiers are painted white.",
        174: "A mainstay mobile suit of the Space Revolutionary Army, this is Lancerow Dawell's personal unit.\nIt differs from standard units in appearance by way of the two composite communication antennas fitted to the back of its head and its ivory paint scheme.\nCombined with Lancerow's own skill, it delivers performance approaching that of a Gundam-type unit. In its first battle against the Gundam Double X, it overwhelmed Garrod in every respect - melee combat, shooting accuracy, and mobility alike.",
        175: "A colossal transformable mobile armor dropped by the old Revolutionary Army during the Seventh Space War as part of Operation Lilac.\nThe operation failed and the unit was damaged, but it was secretly repaired and buried underground by Dr. Dorat of the old Revolutionary Army, who was living under the alias of Fort Severn's mayor, Nomoa.\nWith a Newtype pilot aboard, its thirty Wired Beam Cannons can detect enemy movement and unleash an All-Range Attack.",
        176: "A mobile suit developed by the old Space Revolutionary Army exclusively for Newtype pilots.\nBeyond its high mobility, its greatest feature is that it is equipped with Bits, brainwave-guided weapons that only a Newtype can use.\nRecords show that at least five or more units were built for Operation Lilac, the Seventh Space War operation aimed at landing on and subjugating Earth.",
        177: "A type of unmanned mobile suit known as a Bit Mobile Suit, controlled via brainwaves transmitted from a Gundam equipped with the Flash System. Because it corresponds to a Gundam, it is called a G Bit.\nNormally, a G Bit exists for each Gundam that serves as its host, but this particular unit was instead controlled via Psycommu by D.O.M.E. on the moon. Armed with a beam bazooka capable of downing even a Crouda in a single shot, and possessing maneuverability on par with Gundam-type units, it served as the defense system for a microwave transmission facility.",
        178: "The state of the Impulse Gundam, one of ZAFT's new-generation high-performance 'Second Stage Series' units, when equipped with the Force Silhouette.\nNotable features of the Impulse Gundam include the 'Deuterion Beam Transmission System,' which allows remote energy supply from a mother ship, the 'Core Splendor mechanism,' in which the cockpit morphs into a small fighter craft, and the 'Silhouette System,' which allows the pilot to switch between three types of weapon units to suit the battle situation.\nOf the Impulse Gundam's three configurations, this one boasts especially superior mobility and is capable of independent flight even within the atmosphere, making it the most frequently used.",
        179: "The state of the Impulse Gundam, one of ZAFT's new-generation high-performance 'Second Stage Series' units, when equipped with the Sword Silhouette.\nSpecialized for close combat, its greatest weapon, the massive anti-ship sword Excalibur, can be split apart and dual-wielded, or its hilts joined together to be wielded like a naginata. When necessary, it can also make use of long-range weapons such as a beam rifle.",
        180: "The state of the Impulse Gundam, one of ZAFT's new-generation high-performance 'Second Stage Series' units, when equipped with the Blast Silhouette.\nIt is equipped with numerous weapons emphasizing long-range attack, chief among them the 'Kerberos High-Energy Long-Range Beam Cannon.' Its excessive firepower truly shows its worth not so much in anti-mobile-suit combat as in attacks against warships and enemy bases.",
        181: "A mainstay unit developed as part of ZAFT's new-generation mass-production 'New Millennium Series' of mobile suits.\nThe ZAKU series includes the ZAKU Warrior for regular troops and the ZAKU Phantom for commanding officers. Through the Wizard System, which allows the backpack unit to be swapped out, both offer high versatility, able to adapt to close combat, artillery combat, and high-mobility combat alike.\nThe name ZAKU is an acronym for 'Zaft Armored Keeper of Unity' (one who bears the peace of ZAFT).",
        182: "The state of the ZAKU Warrior, part of ZAFT's new-generation mass-production 'New Millennium Series,' when equipped with the Gunner Wizard artillery unit.\nIts greatest feature, the 'Orthros High-Energy Long-Range Beam Cannon,' is a powerful weapon that, true to its name, boasts both high firepower and tremendous range. In addition to ZAFT's regular soldiers, Dearka also made use of this unit.",
        183: "Lunamaria's personal Gunner ZAKU Warrior.\nUnlike standard units, it is colored primarily in red, her personal color. Why Lunamaria, who is said to be not particularly skilled at shooting, made such frequent use of this equipment remains a mystery.",
        184: "The state of the ZAKU Phantom, part of ZAFT's new-generation mass-production 'New Millennium Series,' when equipped with the high-mobility Blaze Wizard unit.\nThe ZAKU Phantom is primarily a commander's unit; unlike standard machines, it carries a shield on its right shoulder as well, and its head is fitted with a blade antenna to enhance communication and command capabilities.\nThe Blaze Wizard is equipment that improves mobility through thrusters mounted at various points and boosts firepower through built-in missile pods.",
        185: "Ray Za Burrel's personal Blaze ZAKU Phantom.\nColored white to match Ray's pilot suit, it was nicknamed \"the little white monk\" by Neo.\nThough a highly versatile unit capable of operating from space to underwater, it cannot sustain long flights within the atmosphere, and in naval battles it was used almost exclusively for interception from the deck of the Minerva.",
        186: "Dearka Elsman's personal Blaze ZAKU Phantom.\nUnlike standard units, it is colored black. Until now, Dearka had operated machines in their stock colors - the Gunner ZAKU Warrior he first piloted was green, and his beloved Buster Gundam from the previous war was white-beige. This therefore marks the first time he has had a unit painted in his personal color.",
        187: "A unit developed by ZAFT with an emphasis on anti-mobile-suit combat. It once lost a competitive trial against the ZAKU and was rejected, but its performance was later reevaluated, leading to it entering mass production.\nSpecialized for close combat, the arm-mounted shock whip known as the 'Slayer Whip' can be used in various ways beyond restraining enemy mobile suits - it can also scramble electronic equipment or deal direct damage to a pilot.\nThe name GOUF is an acronym for 'Guardian Of Unity Forerunner' (a pioneer who guards unity).",
        188: "Heine Westenfluss's personal GOUF Ignited.\nLike the ZAKU he had piloted just before this, it has been repainted in his personal color, orange.\nIn the battle at the Dardanelles Strait, combined with Heine's skill, it shot down numerous Murasames. It overwhelmed the Gaia Gundam from start to finish as well, but had its right arm severed by the Freedom Gundam, losing its combat capability.",
        189: "Yzak Joule's personal GOUF Ignited.\nIts white-and-blue color scheme, distinct from standard units, calls to mind his former machine, the Duel Gundam.\nIt is a unit well suited to Yzak's preference for close combat.",
        190: "An improved version of the GuAIZ, ZAFT's mainstay mobile suit during the previous war.\nWhile there are no major changes in appearance, it has been fitted with a rail gun at the waist, and its shield, thrusters, and backpack have all been improved, resulting in an overall boost in performance.\nThe R stands for 'Reinforce.'",
        191: "A specially modified version of the GINN High Maneuver Type, a mass-production mobile suit developed by ZAFT during the previous war.\nIt was used by a terrorist attempting to drop Junius Seven onto Earth, interfering with the demolition operation. Because its pilot was a veteran soldier, its movements rivaled even the latest models despite being an old machine. Dearka, who witnessed it firsthand, was thoroughly outmaneuvered and left in awe.",
        192: "A mobile suit developed by ZAFT based on operational data from the DINN.\nWith the ability to morph into a mobile armor form that boosts aerial capability, a head shape designed with air resistance in mind, and an arsenal made up entirely of ranged weapons, it is a unit specialized for aerial combat.",
        193: "A mass-production mobile suit developed by improving the Earth Alliance Forces' Strike Dagger.\nIt inherits the Strike Dagger's greatest feature, the 'Striker Pack' weapon-swapping system. This allows it to achieve high versatility by switching between packs such as the Jet Striker Pack, which enables atmospheric flight, and the Doppelhorn Pack for long-range attacks, depending on the situation.\nA differently colored variant, the Dark Dagger L, also exists.",
        194: "A fighter-type space mobile armor developed by the Earth Alliance Forces.\nThe successor to the Moebius Zero, it is equipped with four of the wired-type 'Gun Barrel' units, armed with beam cannons and beam edges. This is a weapon that only someone with exceptional spatial awareness can handle, but its pilot, Neo, wields it as naturally as his own limbs, holding his own without any trouble even against Shinn and Ray simultaneously.",
        195: "The Earth Alliance Forces' mainstay mass-production mobile suit, succeeding the Dagger-L.\nIt is highly mobile thanks to large thrusters mounted on its shoulders, back, and legs. Because it can make use of the 'Striker Pack System' from the Dagger-L, the generational transition was able to proceed smoothly.\nIn addition to the Jet Striker Pack, which enables flight even under gravity, there also exists a Multi Striker Pack equipped with nuclear missiles.",
        196: "Neo Roanoke's personal Windam, colored purple unlike standard units.\nWhile the unit's base performance is unchanged from a standard model, its Jet Striker Pack is a special limiter-removed specification, giving it a substantial boost in thrust.\nSince it lacked weaponry that could take advantage of Neo's true forte - his spatial awareness - it saw no particularly flashy exploits, but it nevertheless held its own, and more, against both Shinn and Athrun.",
        197: "A mobile suit developed as one of ZAFT's new-generation high-performance 'Second Stage Series' units.\nOne of three new-model Gundams stolen from the military PLANT Armory One by the Earth Alliance Forces' special unit Phantom Pain. Because of this, it carries designation numbers from both ZAFT (ZGMF-X24S) and the Alliance (RGX-01).\nWith large thrusters on its back and waist, it is a unit specialized for combat in open space, capable of independent flight even within the atmosphere using that same output. Its mobility increases further after morphing into mobile armor form.\nIts distinctive armament includes Mobile Armament Pods based on an improved DRAGOON System, which allow it to carry out an All-Range Attack. Using this, it instantly wiped out two GuAIZ R units from the Minerva that had been sent in pursuit from Armory One.",
        198: "A mobile suit developed as one of ZAFT's new-generation high-performance 'Second Stage Series' units.\nOne of three new-model Gundams stolen from the military PLANT Armory One by the Earth Alliance Forces' special unit Phantom Pain. Because of this, it carries designation numbers from both ZAFT (ZGMF-X31S) and the Alliance (RGX-02).\nA highly versatile unit usable in a variety of battle conditions, it performs at its absolute best in underwater combat. When it morphs into its uniquely shaped mobile armor form, it can swim freely underwater like a fish returned to water. It once toyed with Ray's and Lunamaria's ZAKUs simultaneously and sank the submarine carrier Nilagongo, among other feats.",
        199: "A mobile suit developed as one of ZAFT's new-generation high-performance 'Second Stage Series' units.\nOne of three new-model Gundams stolen from the military PLANT Armory One by the Earth Alliance Forces' special unit Phantom Pain. Because of this, it carries designation numbers from both ZAFT (ZGMF-X88S) and the Alliance (RGX-03).\nFollowing in the design lineage of the BuCUE and LaGOWE, it can morph into a four-legged beast-type mobile armor form. Specialized for ground-based melee combat, its basic tactic is to close the distance on enemies using its mobility and agility, then cut them down with its wing-shaped beam blades.",
        200: "A mobile suit developed as one of ZAFT's new-generation high-performance 'Second Stage Series' units.\nOne of three new-model Gundams stolen from the military PLANT Armory One by the Earth Alliance Forces' special unit Phantom Pain.\nThis unit was recovered by ZAFT after being disabled in combat against the Savior Gundam and the Impulse Gundam. During its transport back to PLANT, the Clyne Faction apparently pulled some strings, and it ended up being sent to the Eternal instead. It was subsequently repainted in a coloring reminiscent of the LaGOWE and became Waltfeld's personal unit.",
        201: "A mobile suit developed as one of ZAFT's new-generation high-performance 'Second Stage Series' units. It was entrusted to Athrun by Durandal when he was appointed to FAITH.\nSpecialized for aerial combat, it gains even greater mobility by morphing into mobile armor form, which also enables long-range cruising. It served as a mainstay unit for the Minerva, which fought frequently at sea.\nIn battle, it can use hit-and-run tactics that exploit its high mobility, as well as attacks that vary in speed to confuse the enemy.",
        202: "ZAFT's most advanced mobile suit, developed to bring a decisive end to the war against the Earth Alliance Forces.\nAs Shinn's abilities grew rapidly, Durandal came to believe that the Impulse Gundam could no longer make full use of his talent, and had fine adjustments made to the unit, effectively making it Shinn's personal machine.\nIt is equipped with the 'Hyper Deuterion,' a power plant that combines a nuclear engine with the Deuterion Beam Transmission System, and can generate wings of light from its wing parts to achieve tremendous mobility.\nIt combines all the strengths of the Impulse Gundam's three configurations, successfully achieving both a varied arsenal effective at any range and outstanding maneuverability. Further equipped with unique systems such as palm-mounted beam cannons and a Mirage-Colloid-based Double function, it realizes the concept of a single unit capable of handling any battle situation.",
        203: "The most advanced mobile suit, an evolution of the Providence Gundam developed in the closing days of the previous war.\nIt was originally intended to be given to Athrun, from whom great things were expected, but when Athrun himself attempted to defect from ZAFT, Ray, who pursued him, ended up piloting it instead - and it became his machine from then on.\nThe 'DRAGOON System' mounted on its back has improved response thanks to an upgraded quantum interface, allowing it to be used regardless of the pilot's spatial awareness. In outer space, it shows its true worth by detaching from the main body to carry out an All-Range Attack. Within the atmosphere, it remains attached and instead adjusts its angle, enabling multiple attacks across all 360 degrees.",
        204: "A mobile suit developed by ZAFT in the closing days of the previous war and entrusted by Lacus to Kira. It was heavily damaged in battle against the Providence Gundam during the final battle of that war, but was secretly repaired in Orb and kept in strict storage deep within an underground shelter.\nThough an older machine, it is equipped with a Neutron Jammer Canceller, technology now banned from installation in mobile suits. Because it uses a nuclear fusion engine for power, it has no limit on operating time, giving it performance that can overwhelm current-generation units. Kira, who wished to avoid further fighting, kept it sealed away, but was ultimately forced to pilot it again in order to protect Lacus and those around her from an assassination squad. Since then it has operated together with the Archangel, used only to strip enemies of their mobility and combat capability.",
        205: "The most advanced mobile suit, developed alongside the Infinite Justice Gundam at the 'Factory,' the base of the anti-Durandal Clyne Faction.\nIt has a gold frame housing a new type of power plant, the laser fusion engine, giving it output several times that of the Freedom Gundam. Its newly added 'Super DRAGOON Mobile Weapon System' allows the mobility-enhancing wing sections to detach and be used as wirelessly guided beam weapons. In its first sortie, it made a spectacular debut using this new weapon, disabling a combined total of twenty-five ZAKUs and GOUFs in just two minutes.\nIts armor has also been changed to VPS Armor, and it even has a built-in beam shield, making it a unit with no weak point to exploit in either offense or defense. If it has any single flaw, it is that its performance is so high that no one but Kira can handle it.\nIts official name is 'Strike Freedom Gundam,' but Kira consistently called it simply 'Freedom.'",
        206: "The most advanced mobile suit, developed alongside the Strike Freedom Gundam at the 'Factory,' the base of the anti-Durandal Clyne Faction.\nAn evolution of the Justice Gundam that Athrun piloted during the previous war, it also incorporates technology from ZAFT's 'Second Stage Series.' It carries a laser fusion engine within a silver frame, and its greatest feature, the combined thruster-and-weapon unit 'Fatum-01,' has also received major reinforcement and improvement.\nBoth the unit itself and Fatum-01 are equipped with numerous close-quarters melee weapons, and when used as an assault weapon it dealt a fatal blow to the Minerva's propulsion system. In the final battle it was used against the interior of Requiem, successfully destroying it.",
        207: "A mobile suit left to Cagalli by Uzumi Nara Athha, Orb's former Chief Representative.\nDevelopment had been underway since the previous war, but because the latest technology was incorporated at every stage, it was ultimately completed as a high-performance unit that rivals current-generation mobile suits.\nThe Oowashi (Golden Eagle) Equipment is optimized for operation within the atmosphere, with an attached flight unit enabling independent flight. High-energy beam cannons mounted on either side give it strong long-range attack capability.\nIts dazzling golden body is the 'Yatanokagami,' an anti-beam defense and reflection system that absorbs beams fired at the unit, locks onto the attacking enemy, and reflects the beam back at them. This grants it high defensive power as well as the ability to turn an opponent's own attack directly into a counterattack. However, it has the weakness of being unable to fully guard against solid projectile weapons.",
        208: "A mobile suit left to Cagalli by Uzumi Nara Athha, Orb's former Chief Representative.\nWhen it was taken up into space, Neo took over as pilot in place of Cagalli, who had to remain in Orb.\nThe Shiranui Equipment is optimized for operation in space, and its greatest feature is the 'Guided Mobile Beam Turret System,' an adaptation of the DRAGOON System designed so that anyone can use it. Neo, who already possessed superior spatial awareness, handled it with complete freedom - on offense, destroying numerous enemy mobile suits at once, and on defense, linking the beam turrets together to form a barrier.",
        209: "Orb's next-generation mass-production mobile suit, developed by Morgenroete. It is the successor to the M1 Astray and retains traces of its predecessor's design in the shape of its head.\nDesigned with carrier-based operation in mind, it can take either a general-purpose mobile suit form or a high-mobility fighter jet form. Despite being a mass-production unit, its base performance is by no means low, and it is a well-balanced machine overall. Thanks to the resolve and unity of the Orb forces, it performed beyond its specifications.",
        210: "Andrew Waltfeld's personal Murasame.\nIt is distinguished by its yellow coloring, though its performance is the same as a standard unit.\nIt sortied in the Battle of the Dardanelles Strait, where Waltfeld, quipping \"I'm not as good as Kira,\" shot down numerous Murasames with it.",
        211: "A prototype mobile armor developed by the Earth Alliance Forces.\nIts crab-like silhouette and sheer size overwhelm anyone who faces it. Indeed, the Minerva's bridge crew - Arthur in particular - were considerably shaken the first time they laid eyes on it.\nIt possesses mobility unimaginable for its massive frame, and can attack in all directions using its claws and beam cannons. It is also a formidable unit capable of deploying a positron reflector on its front to bounce back even the Minerva's Tannhauser cannon. However, to make full use of its capabilities, it requires a crew of three - a captain, a helmsman, and a gunner.",
    },
}
